  "description": "Curated reference for Global Workspace Theory (Baars 1988) and its neural instantiation Global Neuronal Workspace (Dehaene & Changeux, 2001-2020). Consciousness is identified with the brain-wide broadcast (ignition) of content from competing specialised processors into a capacity-limited workspace. Includes architecture, neural correlates (P3b, late gamma, frontoparietal ignition), spiking model, the front-vs-back debate, COGITATE adversarial findings, and bridges to FEP/IIT/AST/EFC.",
